Z||000000||Richard Parnell||10-18-2001||02:20 AM||||Hello- Haven't been to the site for a while.  I was wondering if the v8 kit parts (adapterplate etc) would work for a 383.  I have been talking with a guy about building a 383 with 450 crank and 350 heads.  Will everything match up or will I need to make diff mods, ie the wtr pump etc.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Nashco||10-18-2001||02:32 AM||||Actually, I'm pretty sure the 383 is a 350 with a 400 crank.  This is the same as a regular 350 externally, only modified internals to give it more stroke.  Anybody correct me if I'm wrong, but I feel confident on this one <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>So, to answer your question, yes, all of the parts will work exactly the same as on the 350.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Stage-2GT||10-18-2001||06:39 AM||||Talk to Tina, I think she has the 383 in hers.<P>S2GT <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000003||mrfixit58||10-18-2001||07:16 AM||||If a SBC 383 (i.e., a 350 with a stroked 400 crank) the the only difference is the size of the dampener on the front of the crank. 400 cranks are externally balanced.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tina||10-18-2001||11:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Richard Parnell:<BR><B> I have been talking with a guy about building a 383 with 450 crank and 350 heads. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Let me know how that 450 crank works in your 350.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"><BR>Actually there is a forged crankshaft for making a 383 internally balanced, so Archies crank pulley can be used, it costs about $600 and uses 6 inch connecting rods.<P>Eric||||reg||1
Z||000005||Richard Parnell||10-19-2001||03:50 AM||||Thanks for the info all. Tina, what kind of hp do you get w/yours?||||reg||6
Z||000006||Tina||10-19-2001||05:08 PM||||Sorry, still don't have the answer to that.<BR>Hopefully this winter, I'll have time to cart the engine to a dyno.<BR>It's been on my "To do List" for quite a while now,along with <BR>...Taking it to the Dragstrip...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011008.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011008.html</A> <BR>That I did manage to get done.<BR>Now if I only to be able to drive it right, there <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Later Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||MinnGreenGT||10-19-2001||05:17 PM||||Let's see... using the simple HP calculator ( <A HREF="http://www.clubdsm.com/tools/calchp.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.clubdsm.com/tools/calchp.htm</A>  ) based on Tina's trap speed of 106.95mph, and an approximate weight of 2800lbs (roughly the weight of a coupe+80lbs for the V8) and a ET of 12.931... it comes up with an estimate of 256-267hp. (I'm assuming this is supposed to be RWHP).  <P>I know that's low for the 383, and if you read Tina's post about running at the track, you know her runs weren't perfect (neither is this mathmatical calculation...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  So re-estimate a 12.5 run, it gives back around 283... still seems low.  Oh well, figured I'd give it a try!<P>Does it really matter now... Tina's car kicks butt, and that's all there really is to it!  L8tr Tina-<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Immortal||10-19-2001||08:20 PM||||12.9 in 1/4 mile with street tires NO WAY. Even with a SBC in it.<P>Are you sure it was not a 1/8th mile track ?||||reg||13
Z||000009||Hartz||10-19-2001||08:31 PM||||Immortal - 12.9 with a setup like Tina's is completely believable.  My car pulled a 13.3 with a mostly stock 350 TPI motor on cheap 215 street tires.  I suspect Tina's car is easily capable of mid-12's. <P>Keep in mind these are light little cars...<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||10-19-2001||09:00 PM||||I just recently purchased John Lingenfelters book on how to rebuild a small block.<P>In the book it says you don't need a 400 crank to make a 383.. I was kind of suprised when I read this. Any ideas??<P>12.9 On street tires is very believable!! Look at weight distribution , all your weight is over the rear wheels! All that low end TQ created by the extra cubes. Plus your only pushing around 2750 or so. Good power to weight ratio. <P>I don't think Immortal has heard of 1FST2M6 yet...a automatic 2.8 running NOS to the tune of 12.920's on street tires!.<P><BR>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Immortal||10-19-2001||09:05 PM||||Light little cars + street tires + 350 tpi= alot of tire burn. In turn loss of time, loss of HP and loss of speed.<P>12's are out of the question, not even with a 427Ci 350 HP||||reg||1
